[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue. Run through `causes.ts`, its reports
come from two different problems. The table below is built from the export at render time.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The two problems

- **parser**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Tenants whose people write the
  day first see a flipped date. This is the bug #4471 describes.
- **hint**: tenants on `booking-v3` print `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, so their
  day-first people type month first and the form reads it the tenant's way. This is a form
  bug, a different fix, and it has no ticket of its own on #4471.

The five reports the desk read as a one-day move stay counted under `parser`, as the note
under the table says.

## What the desk decided

The desk's update on #4471: the parser problem is fixed, the hint problem will not be fixed
because `booking-v3` is retired.

